WEBVTT

NOTE English visual guide. Editorial descriptions of on-screen concepts; no spoken narration.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Neural networks require numbers, so a text pipeline must turn symbols into usable numerical

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
representations.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.400
Tokenization divides text into units, such as words, subwords or characters.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.600
A vocabulary assigns each token an integer ID. Larger IDs do not mean larger or more important

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.200
meanings.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.400
A one-hot vector marks one vocabulary position with one and all others with zero. It encodes

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.800
identity but no built-in semantic similarity.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
A large vocabulary makes these identity vectors wide and sparse.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.800
An embedding table stores a shorter, dense vector for each token ID.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.800
Looking up an ID selects its row. The embedding values are learned parameters that can receive

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:07.600
gradients during training.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.000
A prediction task supplies a learning signal. Tokens used in similar ways can develop useful

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.000
relationships in the learned space.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:26.000
A two-dimensional plot is a simplified view of vectors that usually have many more coordinates.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Nearby vectors may reflect useful similarities. Individual dimensions need not correspond to

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.000
human-readable concepts.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Vector arithmetic can illustrate relationships, but analogy patterns depend on the training data and

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.000
objective.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.600
Cosine similarity compares directions: dot product divided by the product of vector lengths. Values

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.200
range from minus one to one for nonzero vectors.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Aligned directions have cosine one; perpendicular directions have cosine zero. Opposite directions

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.000
have cosine minus one, without guaranteeing opposite meanings.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.800
Averaging token vectors produces a simple text representation but discards token order.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Static lookup gives a token the same starting vector in different sentences. Contextual models

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.000
update its representation using surrounding information.
